findings.proposed:
1) src/future-autopsy/lib/autopsy-data.ts: delete the hard-coded opening sentence from all eight CAUSE_LEADS strings (lines 123, 125 'No champion is recorded. '; 129, 131 'No economic buyer is recorded. '; 135, 137 'Fewer than three stakeholders are recorded. '; 141, 143 'The deal hasn't been updated recently. ') so each lead is only the pattern and the advice. 2) src/future-autopsy/lib/autopsy.ts lines 79-82: open the paragraph with the evidence sentence the cause engine already computed for this deal, and use the champion / economic-buyer lead only when that field is actually empty:

const top = causes[0];
const namedButBrief =
    (top?.id === "no_champion" && vitals.gates.champion !== "missing") ||
    (top?.id === "no_eb" && vitals.gates.eb !== "missing");
const riskLead = top
    ? `${top.label} ${stageLead(vitals.stageRaw, namedButBrief ? "" : top.id)}`
    : "Nothing in the deal record matches a known risk pattern right now. Keep a dated next step on the calendar so it stays that way.";

(top.label is 'No champion is recorded.' only when the field is empty — causes.ts:112.) Add a regression test in autopsy.test.ts: champion 'Rafael Ibanez', stage negotiation → loseStory does not contain 'No champion is recorded'. OWNER DECISION: stop treating a named champion or economic buyer as missing at all — fire no_champion / no_eb only when the field is empty, or drop the 20-character test in vitals.ts gate(). That changes risk scores, which risk factors and corrective actions are listed, and the order of deals, so it is a product decision.

Generation-only change; which rules fire and all scores stay as they are. a) causes.ts evidenceFor(): after the two existing 'missing' returns (lines 112-113) add
    if (rule.id === "no_champion") return `A champion is named (${vitals.champion}), but the record does not say what their role is or what they have agreed to do.`;
    if (rule.id === "no_eb") return `An economic buyer is named (${vitals.economicBuyer}), but the record does not say how they are involved in the decision.`;
b) autopsy.ts generateAutopsy(): build `chapters` and `winConditions` from `causes.filter((c) => !(c.id === "no_champion" && vitals.gates.champion === "weak"))` so the named-champion case shows one Champion row (the champion_weak row, whose pattern fits) and one win condition; leave `causes` itself untouched for task scoring and routing. c) autopsy-data.ts: give chapterFor a second economic-buyer pattern used when gates.eb === "weak": "A budget owner who is named but has not been part of the conversation often shows up late with new questions. Confirm that this person controls the budget and get them into a conversation before contract time." OWNER DECISION: same as the previous finding (whether a short name should count as a risk factor at all).

autopsy.ts lines 92-98: print only real, distinct conditions and drop the tail when there are none:

const real = winConditions.filter((w) => !w.id.startsWith("momentum_")).slice(0, 3);
const correctedTail = real.length > 0
    ? " For this deal, that means: " + real.map((w) => w.story).join(" ") + " Getting these in place lowers the risk; it doesn't guarantee a close."
    : "";

(AutopsyDoc.winConditions keeps its five entries — autopsy.test.ts:43 asserts length >= 5.) Also autopsy-data.ts:82 momentum_restored → "The buyer has confirmed what has to happen for the deal to move forward, and by when." (it mirrors the advice given for that factor and no longer repeats thread_reactivated at :89, 'Recent buyer activity is recorded.').

causes.ts: pass `prefs` into evidenceFor() and add
    if (rule.id === "stage_stuck") return `The deal has been in ${vitals.stage} for ${vitals.stageAgeDays} days; deals are flagged after ${prefs.stageStuckDays} days in one stage.`;
(keep line 77 as the fallback text but reword it: "The deal has been in its current stage for more than three weeks.")
